bionic shim: the file-mode heal leaves read-only files alone

macapk_heal_app_data_modes walks the app's data directory at every start and
gave owner read+write back to any regular file missing either bit. A file its
owner can read but not write is not the va_arg poison the heal exists for (0000,
0300): it is deliberate. On API 34 dynamically loaded code must be read-only, so
an app marks a downloaded module File.setReadOnly() and refuses it when it is
writable again. Instagram 455 threw "Downloaded module file must be read only"
for every downloaded module at every launch (pytorch, executorch), and its Mantle
module download reported failure.

Only a file the owner cannot read is healed now. After: 0 such errors, the
modules stay 0444 across launches and load ("Split loaded: executorch").

diff --git a/runtime/translator/src/bionic_shim.cpp b/runtime/translator/src/bionic_shim.cpp
--- a/runtime/translator/src/bionic_shim.cpp
+++ b/runtime/translator/src/bionic_shim.cpp
@@ -41828,8 +41930,15 @@ static bool macapk_is_proc_pid_file(const std::string& s, const char* name) {
 // disk). Even with the open() fix, OPENING an existing mode-0000 file returns
 // EACCES (no perms for anyone, incl. owner), so the fixed code would still
 // inherit the poisoned tree -> the UnauthorizedAccessException storm persists.
-// Walk the app data dir once and restore owner rwx where it is missing (files
+// Walk the app data dir once and restore owner access where it is missing (files
 // 0644, dirs 0755); files already sane are skipped. Idempotent; runs once.
+//
+// A file the owner can READ but not write is not poison, it is deliberate: on
+// API 34 dynamically loaded code must be read-only, so an app marks a
+// downloaded module File.setReadOnly() and refuses to load it once it is
+// writable again (Instagram 455: "Downloaded module file must be read only",
+// every launch, for each of its downloaded modules). Only a file its owner
+// cannot read is healed -- the observed poison (0000, 0300) always is one.
 static void macapk_heal_app_data_modes() {
     const char* root = __macapk_get_android_root();
     const char* sub  = __macapk_get_data_subdir();
@@ -41841,7 +41950,7 @@ static void macapk_heal_app_data_modes() {
                 if ((sb->st_mode & 0700) != 0700)
                     chmod(fp, (sb->st_mode & ~(mode_t)0777) | 0755);
             } else if (S_ISREG(sb->st_mode)) {
-                if ((sb->st_mode & 0600) != 0600)
+                if ((sb->st_mode & 0400) == 0)
                     chmod(fp, (sb->st_mode & ~(mode_t)0777) | 0644);
             }
             return 0;
